SCOPE (honesty covenant: no scope-narrowing, no stubs as final, ADR-011)
  Web SafetyPage.tsx hosts the deterministic, AI-OFF-safe explainer LISTING of every
  safety-related TeslaSync setting from useSettings(). The thin page manifest record
  lists only the 6 chrome strings + GlassPanel1 + the success state, but a header-only
  screen would be a stub. The FULL deterministic surface is reproduced natively:
    - page chrome (PageContainer title + subtitle),
    - the single GlassPanel listing (GlassPanel1): header (title + subtitle),
    - ALL SEVEN setting rows (title + current-value Badge + plain-English explanation
      + per-row "Docs" link), reproducing every anonymous region of the web <ul>,
    - the read-only change-hint footer.
  The opt-in <AISafetySettingExplainer> panel is ABSENT from the web DOM in the default
  ai_mode='off' state (the page's documented "ShowsStaticHelpOnly" invariant) and is a
  separate, gated component parity unit — correctly OUT of this PAGE's scope (its
  inclusion as a non-functional panel would itself be a stub). The deterministic listing
  IS the page's default/safe surface, reproduced in full.

DECISIONS
  - Routing: web App.tsx routes /settings/safety as a standalone, deep-linkable route
    OUTSIDE the sidebar nav config (it is reached from the in-page link / a direct URL).
    Reproducing it as a sidebar item would be an ANTI-parity addition, so — per the
    accepted TeslaSync/Features sibling precedent (Geofences / TirePressure / GuardMode)
    — the page ships as a NavigationStack-ready View + a typed NavigationDestination
    (SafetySettingsLink + .safetySettingsDestination()) + a SafetyRouteRegistration.make()
    factory, rather than editing the shared AppRoute sidebar enum. No phantom sidebar entry.
  - Strings: the catalog already carries the web i18n bundle under the i18next default
    namespace prefix `translation.` — all 24 translation.safetySettings.* keys are present
    with en values IDENTICAL to the web defaults verbatim (the 6 required chrome keys + the
    14 row keys + 4 aiExplainer keys). The page binds these (suffix == web key name),
    matching the dominant TeslaSync/Features convention (GuardMode, 172 call sites). Value
    chips reuse translation.common.{on,off,active}; 4 NEW scoped value keys were added for
    Suspended + digest Instant/Hourly/Daily. Zero hardcoded user-facing literals.
  - States: loading (panel header + ProgressView) → success (listing). The deterministic
    listing has no empty/error surface (web useSettings() always yields DEFAULT_SETTINGS),
    so it never blanks; the model falls back to web defaults rather than showing an error.
  - Value badge: a feature-local SafetyValueBadge mirrors TSBadge's .info visual via the
    shared Color.TS.statusInfo token, because the value is dynamic (a localized token OR a
    verbatim HH:MM/em-dash datum) while the shared TSBadge accepts only a static key
    (and is out of this prompt's allowed-files scope to edit).

FILES (in scope)
  A apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Settings/SafetyPage.swift               (View + SafetyValueBadge + previews)
  A apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Settings/SafetyPageModel.swift          (@Observable model, seam, kind enum, value)
  A apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Settings/SafetyRouteRegistration.swift  (typed NavigationDestination + factory)
  M apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings                         (+4 value keys; the 6 PARITY keys pre-present)
  M apps/parity/apple-ledger.json                                         (+ apple-macos & apple-ios rows, done 8/8)

ADAPTIVE / HIG / a11y / units
  - macOS/iPad (regular): each row lays its main block + "Docs" link side-by-side.
    iPhone (compact, horizontalSizeClass): stacked (web sm:grid-cols-[1fr_auto]).
    Reading column capped (web PageContainer max-width); driven by @Observable model
    (ADR-004, no networking in the view).
  - Materials via TSGlassPanel; tokens-only color/typography (P2) — TSPageTitle,
    TSSectionTitle, Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing; no hand-rolled glass.
  - VoiceOver: combined row elements; each "Docs" link labelled "<setting> — Docs" via
    Text concatenation. Dynamic Type (system fonts), light/dark + increased-contrast via
    tokens, ≥44pt Link targets.
  - Units: N/A for this page (no SI quantities; quiet-hours are HH:MM clock strings shown
    verbatim exactly as the web stores them — formatted only at the display boundary).

